  Thing shrine_door_b "the shrine door" at green_b {
    State open "The shrine door stands ajar on its dim candle, as it has always stood.".
    State chained "A length of chain has been looped through the shrine door's rings and padlocked. Someone has hung a card on it, in a priest's careful capitals: CLOSED FOR THE PRESERVATION OF ORDER.".
  }
  Initially Assert state(shrine_door_b, open).
  Observe camp_view_b at camp_b as feature when true "A yard behind the inn's stable, given over to the Walk: straw on the ground in rows, fire-rings of ash-wood, staves stacked in threes against the wall, and a line of washed heel-cloths drying on a rope. Whoever is in charge sits where the draught is least. A number is chalked above every door.".
  Observe stone_view_b at station_b as feature when true "The Station is a roofed rest beside an old milestone: three posts and a slate roof, a stone bench, and the milestone itself, a squat grey column with the Office's wheel cut in the top and a number cut below it that was recut, in a newer hand, over an older number. Ash from a hundred small fires lies in the bench's corners.".

